{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04Z2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$p : \\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$p' : \\mathcal{S}' \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$F : \\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathcal{S}'$", "MATH_0005": "$1$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{I}_{\\mathcal{S}/\\mathcal{S}'}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0009": "$(x, \\alpha)$", "MATH_0010": "$x \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{S})$", "MATH_0011": "$\\alpha : x \\to x$", "MATH_0012": "$F(\\alpha) = \\text{id}$", "MATH_0013": "$(x, \\alpha) \\to (y, \\beta)$", "MATH_0014": "$\\phi : x \\to y$", "MATH_0015": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nx\\ar[r]_\\phi\\ar[d]_\\alpha &\ny\\ar[d]^{\\beta} \\\\\nx\\ar[r]^\\phi &\ny \\\\\n}\n$$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{I}_{\\mathcal{S}/\\mathcal{S}'} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0017": "$(x, \\alpha) \\mapsto p(x)$", "MATH_0018": "$$\n\\mathcal{I}_{\\mathcal{S}/\\mathcal{S}'} \\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{S}\n\\times_{\\Delta, (\\mathcal{S} \\times_{\\mathcal{S}'} \\mathcal{S}), \\Delta}\n\\mathcal{S}\n$$", "MATH_0019": "$(2, 1)$", "MATH_0020": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0021": "$\\mathcal{I}_{\\mathcal{S}/\\mathcal{S}'}$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0006": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0007": "\\item", "STRUCT_0008": "\\item", "STRUCT_0009": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-inertia-fibred-category}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:02307e9fd773a3a52d7127e39affc4db36c5a48236a5ea045a58a85d5646f4b1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:641996ecd1597b78702fa93859c29e2ddec162f7e6cde30b9811cc58fde9d165", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category. Let\n<MATH_0002> and\n<MATH_0003> be fibred categories.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a <MATH_0005>-morphism of\nfibred categories over <MATH_0006>. Consider the category\n<MATH_0007> over <MATH_0008> whose\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> objects are pairs <MATH_0009> where <MATH_0010>\nand <MATH_0011> is an automorphism with <MATH_0012>,\n<STRUCT_0003> morphisms <MATH_0013> are given by morphisms\n<MATH_0014> such that\n<MATH_0015>\ncommutes, and\n<STRUCT_0004> the functor <MATH_0016>\nis given by <MATH_0017>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nThen\n<STRUCT_0006>\n<STRUCT_0007> there is an equivalence\n<MATH_0018>\nin the <MATH_0019>-category of categories over <MATH_0020>, and\n<STRUCT_0008> <MATH_0021> is a fibred category over\n<MATH_0022>.\n<STRUCT_0009>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e7dd4e5e44dadcd2f7f66285103121000a99fc3438e7ead2d78c2fe827451a11", "unit_id": "tag:034H:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04Z2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$2$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{S}\n\\times_{\\Delta, (\\mathcal{S} \\times_{\\mathcal{S}'} \\mathcal{S}), \\Delta}\n\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0003": "$(x, y, (\\iota, \\kappa))$", "MATH_0004": "$x$", "MATH_0005": "$y$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0007": "$(\\iota, \\kappa) : (x, x, \\text{id}_{F(x)}) \\to (y, y, \\text{id}_{F(y)})$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{S} \\times_{\\mathcal{S}'} \\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\iota, \\kappa : x \\to y$", "MATH_0010": "$F(\\iota) = F(\\kappa)$", "MATH_0011": "$$\nI_{\\mathcal{S}/\\mathcal{S}'}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{S}\n\\times_{\\Delta, (\\mathcal{S} \\times_{\\mathcal{S}'} \\mathcal{S}), \\Delta}\n\\mathcal{S}\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$(x, \\alpha)$", "MATH_0013": "$(x, x, (\\alpha, \\text{id}_x))$", "MATH_0014": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0015": "$(\\phi, \\phi)$", "MATH_0016": "$$\n\\mathcal{S}\n\\times_{\\Delta, (\\mathcal{S} \\times_{\\mathcal{S}'} \\mathcal{S}), \\Delta}\n\\mathcal{S}\n\\longrightarrow\nI_{\\mathcal{S}/\\mathcal{S}'}\n$$", "MATH_0017": "$(x, y, (\\iota, \\kappa))$", "MATH_0018": "$(x, \\kappa^{-1} \\circ \\iota)$", "MATH_0019": "$(\\phi, \\phi') : (x, y, (\\iota, \\kappa)) \\to (z, w, (\\lambda, \\mu))$", "MATH_0020": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0021": "$I_{\\mathcal{S}/\\mathcal{S}'}$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{S}\n\\times_{\\Delta, (\\mathcal{S} \\times_{\\mathcal{S}'} \\mathcal{S}), \\Delta}\n\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0023": "$$\n(\\text{id}_x, \\kappa) :\n(x, x, (\\kappa^{-1} \\circ \\iota, \\text{id}_x))\n\\longrightarrow\n(x, y, (\\iota, \\kappa)).\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-2-product-fibred-categories-over-C}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-fibred-equivalent}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-2-product-fibred-categories-over-C}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:474d0d253d39cf65d5855d50d65e186f6f5484e0bd0e49fec758c6db08b8e369", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f76e77f40477f8ee0296de5a5a9ca7115f47702d7989cc6ddb30ab7663bba399", "source_text": "Note that (2) follows from (1) by\nLemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>. Thus it suffices to prove (1).\nWe will use without further mention the construction of the <MATH_0001>-fibre product\nfrom\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nIn particular an object of\n<MATH_0002>\nis a triple <MATH_0003> where <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005> are objects of\n<MATH_0006>, and\n<MATH_0007>\nis an isomorphism in <MATH_0008>.\nThis just means that <MATH_0009> are isomorphisms and that\n<MATH_0010>. Consider the functor\n<MATH_0011>\nwhich to an object <MATH_0012> of the left hand side assigns the object\n<MATH_0013> of the right hand side\nand to a morphism <MATH_0014> of the left hand side\nassigns the morphism <MATH_0015> of the right hand side.\nWe claim that a quasi-inverse to that morphism is given by the\nfunctor\n<MATH_0016>\nwhich to an object <MATH_0017> of the left hand side\nassigns the object <MATH_0018> of the right hand side\nand to a morphism\n<MATH_0019>\nof the left hand side assigns the morphism <MATH_0020>.\nIndeed, the endo-functor of <MATH_0021> induced\nby composing the two functors above is the identity on the nose, and\nthe endo-functor induced on\n<MATH_0022>\nis isomorphic to\nthe identity via the natural isomorphism\n<MATH_0023>\nSome details omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:229a3cb183aec813a4a4d59a3aea1957bdb1526df01f3f5b7446b857b0143aa4", "unit_id": "tag:034H:proof"}
